WEBVTT

00:01.810 --> 00:05.230
<i>Raeliana, this is Freese Eriteal.</i>

00:05.820 --> 00:10.490
<i>I know you suffered through a 
terrible experience with the Brooks scandal.</i>

00:10.900 --> 00:13.650
<i>Have you been well since then?</i>

00:14.470 --> 00:19.570
<i>I have enclosed the invitation 
to the gathering that I promised you.</i>

00:20.060 --> 00:21.860
Thanks, Freese!

00:21.860 --> 00:24.310
Now Noah will owe me one!

00:24.880 --> 00:30.030
<i>I look forward to seeing you 
at the monster hunt.</i>

00:33.820 --> 00:37.440
<i>Right, the monster hunt...</i>

00:41.260 --> 00:45.360
<i>A three-day event held every year 
in the Sycret Mountains</i>

00:45.360 --> 00:47.400
<i>in preparation for winter.</i>

00:48.510 --> 00:51.440
<i>Monsters come down from 
the mountains looking for food in winter.</i>

00:51.440 --> 00:55.080
<i>The hunt is a state project held 
to stop them from attacking citizens.</i>

00:56.400 --> 01:00.040
<i>Nobles famous for their 
combat prowess participate,</i>

01:00.040 --> 01:03.760
<i>and they offer the monsters they caught 
to the lady of their choice.</i>

01:04.530 --> 01:09.320
<i>But I'm told Noah has never 
offered his monsters to anyone,</i>

01:09.320 --> 01:12.040
<i>so it has nothing to do with me, right?</i>

01:17.390 --> 01:21.220
<i>These are... the letters 
I wrote to Beatrice?</i>

01:21.700 --> 01:24.050
<i>They were returned? But why?</i>

01:26.880 --> 01:29.420
<i>The name and address are correct.</i>

01:30.060 --> 01:34.320
<i>Was there some reason she 
couldn't receive letters?</i>

01:37.160 --> 01:38.710
<i>Surely not...</i>

03:14.110 --> 03:18.130
<i>Originally, what prompts the protagonist 
Beatrice to return from abroad</i>

03:19.200 --> 03:20.870
<i>is Raeliana's death.</i>

03:21.910 --> 03:24.240
<i>But Raeliana survived.</i>

03:25.680 --> 03:29.270
<i>As things stand, Beatrice will
 never return from abroad,</i>

03:29.270 --> 03:31.220
<i>which is why I sent letters.</i>

03:31.900 --> 03:36.540
<i>I wouldn't think a story change as minor 
as receiving a summons from Raeliana</i>

03:36.540 --> 03:39.090
<i>would have that great an effect.</i>

03:39.720 --> 03:40.950
<i>In fact...</i>

03:42.270 --> 03:46.000
<i>I only acted because my life depended on it.</i>

03:46.000 --> 03:49.050
<i>I never had any intention 
of ruining this story.</i>

03:49.690 --> 03:50.660
<i>Yet...</i>

03:51.480 --> 03:56.960
<i>If my surviving caused some 
fundamental change in the story...</i>

03:58.300 --> 04:00.040
My lady...

04:00.040 --> 04:05.000
y-you have done lovely work... but...

04:05.000 --> 04:06.080
Huh?

04:13.440 --> 04:16.120
If you intend to present it to the duke,

04:16.120 --> 04:20.890
why not use the bamboo-leaf oak 
and birds depicted in his family crest?

04:20.890 --> 04:25.760
Though, to my knowledge, 
the duke has never accepted any handkerchiefs

04:25.760 --> 04:28.840
presented to him by ladies...

04:29.830 --> 04:33.830
<i>I never intended to give it 
to him, actually.</i>

04:33.830 --> 04:39.080
But you are his one 
and only fiancée, after all.

04:39.080 --> 04:41.790
<i>Isn't it normal to have only one of those?!</i>

04:41.790 --> 04:44.880
<i>What kind of scumbag does she think Noah is?</i>

05:13.790 --> 05:17.720
<i>I had heard that he'd be busy 
because of the monster hunt, but...</i>

05:24.800 --> 05:29.690
<i>Still, I've never seen him 
sleeping like this before.</i>

05:33.180 --> 05:36.310
<i>He was born with such good looks.</i>

05:36.680 --> 05:39.760
<i>He could act like he 
enjoys life a little more.</i>

05:40.920 --> 05:45.320
<i>Then again, he is 
the leading male in this story.</i>

05:45.680 --> 05:49.690
<i>In the end, he ends up 
with the female lead in a happy ending.</i>

05:51.320 --> 05:53.370
<i>With Beatrice Tranche.</i>

05:54.780 --> 05:58.080
<i>They first meet as a result 
of a misunderstanding,</i>

05:58.080 --> 05:59.590
<i>giving them a terrible start.</i>

05:59.590 --> 06:02.540
<i>But for some reason, 
Beatrice is drawn to him...</i>

06:09.800 --> 06:13.020
<i>They continue to be met by one 
chance encounter after another,</i>

06:14.410 --> 06:18.960
<i>and then, one windy day, 
as her hair flutters about her face,</i>

06:20.100 --> 06:24.920
<i>Noah suddenly murmurs her name 
as he falls in love with her.</i>

06:24.920 --> 06:26.610
<i>Beatri—</i>

06:25.250 --> 06:26.610
Raeliana.

06:28.080 --> 06:29.350
Huh?

06:31.350 --> 06:32.400
Raeliana?

06:33.870 --> 06:37.280
Uh... I-I was...

06:37.720 --> 06:39.810
<i>What excuse can I even make here?!</i>

06:39.810 --> 06:42.570
<i>He caught me sneaking a look at his face!</i>

06:42.570 --> 06:44.410
<i>That he just looked so 
handsome in his sleep?</i>

06:44.410 --> 06:46.120
<i>No, no, no, no, no!</i>

06:46.800 --> 06:50.290
Are you not feeling well? 
Your face is very red.

06:50.290 --> 06:53.640
That's just... um...

07:04.150 --> 07:06.770
I-It's just hot.

07:09.420 --> 07:11.200
<i>Ouch!</i>

07:11.200 --> 07:13.160
Noah!

07:13.160 --> 07:16.890
Sneaking a look at someone's 
face as they sleep, eh?

07:16.890 --> 07:18.370
Led go ud me.

07:18.370 --> 07:19.670
"Led go ud me"?

07:20.260 --> 07:23.040
Led go ud me... please.

07:24.130 --> 07:25.920
Don't you mean, "I'm sorry"?

07:25.920 --> 07:27.000
<i>What?!</i>

07:27.000 --> 07:30.420
<i>And he watched me when 
I was sleeping before, too!</i>

07:30.420 --> 07:33.420
How did sneaking around like 
that make you feel?

07:35.430 --> 07:38.430
I had no idea you were into such things.

07:38.890 --> 07:41.680
I'm... sorry.

07:42.540 --> 07:43.740
Good enough.

07:46.440 --> 07:47.690
Raeliana?

08:02.300 --> 08:04.200
He's so infuriating!

08:16.840 --> 08:19.480
Not bad at all.

08:22.160 --> 08:24.720
It's extremely cold where you're going.

08:24.720 --> 08:27.120
This is the bare minimum you should wear.

08:28.730 --> 08:33.600
With all this on, I feel 
like summer's already here.

08:33.600 --> 08:37.490
You mustn't underestimate 
how cold it is in those mountains.

08:37.490 --> 08:41.490
In Sycret, people freeze 
to death even in autumn!

08:41.800 --> 08:45.480
<i>I won't even be able to 
eat on my own in all this.</i>

08:49.060 --> 08:52.510
Please place your things here, my lady.

08:52.510 --> 08:56.000
Good morning, my lady.

08:56.440 --> 08:58.480
Good morning, Gideon.

09:00.550 --> 09:03.370
I've heard where I'm going is very cold.

09:03.370 --> 09:08.270
Yes, in Sycret, people freeze 
to death even in autumn.

09:08.660 --> 09:10.530
That again?

09:12.720 --> 09:16.280
Are you sure you won't be coming, Brother?

09:16.280 --> 09:19.310
All the combat veterans will be there.

09:20.040 --> 09:23.040
I only just returned from my trip abroad.

09:23.040 --> 09:24.660
Let me have this break.

09:25.240 --> 09:27.610
I'll be on my way, then.

09:30.040 --> 09:31.740
Take care.

09:36.240 --> 09:39.060
This concludes the opening ceremony.

09:39.400 --> 09:42.300
I wish you all the best of luck.

10:07.560 --> 10:13.080
<i>I guess it doesn't even matter to them 
whether Noah has a fiancée or not.</i>

10:13.080 --> 10:14.470
My lady?

10:15.320 --> 10:19.960
My lady, you're looking very... warm today.

10:20.470 --> 10:22.970
I heard it would be cold here.

10:23.350 --> 10:26.960
Yes, in Sycret, people freeze 
to death even in autumn.

10:27.470 --> 10:30.870
<i>Is that Sycret's official 
slogan or something?</i>

10:30.870 --> 10:32.990
My lady, your hand, please.

10:32.990 --> 10:33.830
Huh?

10:43.360 --> 10:45.970
<i>A vow to a lady?</i>

10:46.620 --> 10:49.600
<i>Will you be participating 
in the hunt, as well?</i>

10:49.600 --> 10:50.530
Yes.

10:50.530 --> 10:52.320
I had no idea...

10:52.320 --> 10:54.320
I didn't make a handkerchief for you.

10:54.320 --> 10:55.950
That's all right.

10:55.950 --> 10:59.240
I didn't come here just 
to receive a handkerchief.

10:59.240 --> 11:00.630
Still...

11:02.140 --> 11:03.120
In that case...

11:12.420 --> 11:14.640
This is enough for me!

11:14.640 --> 11:16.390
Dame Ansley...

11:17.020 --> 11:19.550
Well, wish me luck.

11:20.960 --> 11:22.880
<i>What a dreamboat...</i>

11:23.560 --> 11:24.730
Raeliana...

11:25.530 --> 11:26.550
Raeliana?

11:27.510 --> 11:28.730
Noah...

11:30.550 --> 11:31.740
You look very...

11:31.740 --> 11:33.550
Warm, right?

11:33.550 --> 11:37.350
In Sycret, people freeze 
to death even in autumn.

11:38.800 --> 11:41.760
More importantly, 
aren't you forgetting something?

11:43.140 --> 11:44.620
Oh, right!

11:45.410 --> 11:48.320
Master Taylor, please wait just a moment.

11:48.680 --> 11:50.000
Master Taylor?

11:53.020 --> 11:55.770
Quite gutsy of you to give a handkerchief

11:55.770 --> 11:59.280
to another man right 
in front of your beloved fiancé.

11:59.280 --> 12:01.990
Oh? "Beloved fiancé"?

12:01.990 --> 12:04.530
I do believe you are mistaken.

12:04.530 --> 12:08.320
Should we not at least stick 
to the script we both agreed upon?

12:11.090 --> 12:13.540
What is it you want?

12:13.540 --> 12:15.040
A handkerchief.

12:15.440 --> 12:17.040
I don't have one!

12:17.040 --> 12:18.030
Then what's this?

12:18.490 --> 12:20.100
It's Master Taylor's.

12:20.440 --> 12:22.490
You and your little jokes...

12:22.490 --> 12:24.400
<i>He just never gives up, does he?</i>

12:24.400 --> 12:27.050
I thought it was your policy 
not to accept handkerchiefs.

12:27.050 --> 12:29.800
I'm in the mood to accept one today.

12:29.800 --> 12:32.810
But you turned them down 
from other people earlier!

12:32.810 --> 12:35.800
I want one from my fiancée.

12:37.390 --> 12:39.560
Oh, what shall I do?

12:39.560 --> 12:41.810
I was certain you wouldn't want one.

12:41.810 --> 12:45.320
Then I'll just have to 
accept this one instead.

12:45.320 --> 12:47.080
Give that back!

12:47.080 --> 12:50.090
<i>He's never accepted one before in his life!</i>

12:50.090 --> 12:51.840
<i>Where's this coming from?!</i>

12:54.790 --> 12:56.580
All right, fine.

12:59.580 --> 13:02.890
More importantly, 
aren't you forgetting something?

13:02.890 --> 13:04.590
Am I?

13:12.600 --> 13:15.590
<i>Well, go on! Lower your head already!</i>

13:16.380 --> 13:19.360
Oh, dear. Do forgive me.

13:35.240 --> 13:38.720
<i>What the heck?! 
He could just do it normally!</i>

13:38.720 --> 13:40.250
<i>He's so dramatic!</i>

13:40.250 --> 13:41.240
Here.

13:45.260 --> 13:47.560
Well, do be careful.

14:03.720 --> 14:06.970
<i>Is she asking me to bring back a dragon?</i>

14:14.620 --> 14:16.780
<i>The air is so clean here.</i>

14:17.550 --> 14:22.410
<i>This is my first time leaving the capital 
since I came to this world.</i>

14:22.920 --> 14:28.960
<i>So this is the wall erected by the Granger 
family to protect the front line of Sycret...</i>

14:34.560 --> 14:36.780
Please be careful.

14:37.310 --> 14:40.310
For you, I would give my very life.

14:40.310 --> 14:44.440
They way they're acting, 
you'd think they were going off to war.

14:45.320 --> 14:47.080
<i>Stephanie Carlisle.</i>

14:48.770 --> 14:50.850
<i>Christine Barkley.</i>

14:50.900 --> 14:52.880
It must be their first time.

14:52.880 --> 14:56.030
You must try to understand 
if they seem a bit dramatic.

14:56.030 --> 14:57.670
<i>Vivian Shamal.</i>

14:58.120 --> 15:01.700
<i>They gave Beatrice a rough 
time throughout the novel.</i>

15:08.070 --> 15:09.260
Raeliana!

15:20.080 --> 15:23.470
<i>He's just going to hunt some monsters.
 He'll be fine, right?</i>

15:26.250 --> 15:28.220
Miss McMillan.

15:28.220 --> 15:31.480
Those are the claw marks of a creoder.

15:31.480 --> 15:34.800
<i>The lord of Sycret Castle, Jasper Granger.</i>

15:36.190 --> 15:41.160
It's a terribly fierce monster 
with the appearance of a black lion.

15:41.160 --> 15:45.260
One might call it the true lord 
of the Sycret Mountains.

15:45.260 --> 15:48.780
One day, I will capture it 
with my own hands.

15:48.780 --> 15:50.730
That is my dream.

15:54.800 --> 15:56.700
Miss McMillan...

15:58.280 --> 16:01.010
Please come and have a seat.

16:01.010 --> 16:05.540
I do appreciate the offer, 
but I humbly decline.

16:05.540 --> 16:08.990
<i>I'm not stupid enough to sit beside you.</i>

16:10.080 --> 16:11.770
Well, well!

16:12.540 --> 16:15.940
If it isn't the Duke's fiancée!

16:15.940 --> 16:18.710
You must sit in the center, of course.

16:18.710 --> 16:19.770
Come, now.

16:22.610 --> 16:24.140
Oh, yes!

16:24.140 --> 16:26.780
In the last hunt, Lady Shamal was presented

16:26.780 --> 16:30.870
with three high-ranking monsters, right?

16:30.870 --> 16:33.800
Yes. I look forward to seeing 
how this hunt ends, as well.

16:33.800 --> 16:39.170
I only pray that no one out 
hunting finds themselves in danger.

16:39.720 --> 16:44.300
M-My, how admirable of you, Lady Shamal.

16:45.000 --> 16:46.500
Oh, it's nothing.

16:46.500 --> 16:48.670
<i>Is she happy now?</i>

16:48.670 --> 16:51.870
Um, where is Lady Eriteal?

16:51.870 --> 16:55.570
It seems she's caught a cold 
and won't be joining us.

16:55.800 --> 16:59.480
What about you, Miss McMillan?
 Are you feeling all right?

16:59.480 --> 17:02.300
With the Duke out on the hunt...

17:06.330 --> 17:10.200
<i>What a disgusting attitude. 
She thinks I don't know?</i>

17:10.200 --> 17:12.330
Whatever do you mean?

17:12.330 --> 17:13.480
Oh, my!

17:13.480 --> 17:20.090
Were you not aware that the Duke 
has never offered a monster to anyone before?

17:20.090 --> 17:24.120
Miss McMillan has never been 
a part of the monster hunt before.

17:24.120 --> 17:26.370
Of course she wouldn't know.

17:26.370 --> 17:30.100
And it would seem she didn't 
have anyone to inform her.

17:30.100 --> 17:35.490
Yes, it's true that low-ranking 
women don't usually come to the hunt.

17:36.120 --> 17:38.390
There's nothing else to be done.

17:38.390 --> 17:42.780
We shall have to teach 
Miss McMillan all she needs to know.

17:45.400 --> 17:47.370
I'm quite all right.

17:47.670 --> 17:53.260
Just the fact that the duke accepted 
my handkerchief is enough for me.

17:53.260 --> 17:54.520
Incidentally,

17:54.520 --> 17:59.050
I heard that he's never accepted 
a handkerchief from anyone before.

17:59.050 --> 18:00.750
Is that true?

18:01.230 --> 18:04.340
I don't know the Duke as well as you all do.

18:04.340 --> 18:06.760
It's terribly embarrassing.

18:06.760 --> 18:10.160
So might I ask you to continue 
teaching me so that, little by little,

18:10.160 --> 18:12.070
I might understand things better?

18:13.840 --> 18:18.280
Oh, dear. Have I said something imprudent?

18:21.780 --> 18:23.550
W-Well...

18:23.550 --> 18:26.360
If he hadn't accepted the handkerchief then,

18:26.360 --> 18:30.680
it would put Miss McMillan 
in an awful position as his fiancée.

18:30.680 --> 18:32.210
Y-Yes!

18:32.210 --> 18:36.600
I'm sure he'll bring back 
at least one high-ranking monster.

18:36.600 --> 18:37.640
Yes.

18:38.000 --> 18:41.280
If he truly thinks so fondly of me,

18:41.280 --> 18:45.050
that makes me happier than any number 
of monsters he could bring back.

18:45.600 --> 18:49.060
And don't you think being 
loved by the one you love...

18:51.760 --> 18:56.400
is much better than being 
loved by a hundred others,

18:56.400 --> 18:58.000
Lady Vivian?

18:59.560 --> 19:03.070
Wh-Why do you ask <i>me</i> that?!

19:03.080 --> 19:07.140
I assumed you would understand 
better than all the other ladies.

19:07.710 --> 19:09.590
Am I wrong?

19:09.590 --> 19:11.540
W-Well...

19:12.600 --> 19:15.130
<i>It's common knowledge that Vivian has</i>

19:15.130 --> 19:18.250
<i>been making all kinds 
of intense passes at Noah.</i>

19:19.410 --> 19:20.840
Miss McMillan!

19:20.840 --> 19:23.640
It looks as if your salmon has gone bad!

19:23.640 --> 19:26.850
Get the head chef out here at once!

19:26.850 --> 19:28.130
Huh?

19:28.130 --> 19:32.860
The Duke's fiancée has eaten rotten food!

19:32.860 --> 19:35.100
This is an emergency!

19:35.560 --> 19:37.400
Wh-What are you talking—

19:37.400 --> 19:40.360
Perhaps you should rest in your room?

19:40.360 --> 19:42.270
You mustn't overdo it.

19:43.140 --> 19:44.500
<i>Ugh...</i>

19:52.180 --> 19:54.770
The weather certainly doesn't look good.

19:55.640 --> 19:58.330
<i>I can't see the Wynknight crest.</i>

19:58.690 --> 20:01.320
<i>Did he go that deep into the mountains?</i>

20:01.960 --> 20:04.750
The rain will make it 
difficult to walk, too.

20:05.640 --> 20:10.930
And there are high-ranking monsters 
that are more active in rain.

20:11.810 --> 20:13.920
<i>I have a bad feeling...</i>

20:23.320 --> 20:26.240
Oh, dear! You should have dodged.

20:26.240 --> 20:28.130
Indeed!

20:29.120 --> 20:31.350
<i>These girls again...</i>

20:31.350 --> 20:35.590
I had no idea your vision 
was as poor as your discernment.

20:35.590 --> 20:36.640
Wha—

20:36.640 --> 20:38.710
What do you mean by that?!

20:38.710 --> 20:40.640
Don't feel bad.

20:41.080 --> 20:45.670
Failing to consider your immaturity 
was my own mistake.

20:45.670 --> 20:49.210
<i>Seriously, who does something that childish?</i>

21:03.240 --> 21:05.040
What was that sound?

21:05.040 --> 21:06.930
Ah, right.

21:07.670 --> 21:11.250
It would seem the first group has returned.

21:16.240 --> 21:19.110
That's... an affitee elk, if I'm not mistaken.

21:19.110 --> 21:21.280
A high-ranking monster, I believe.

21:22.260 --> 21:24.860
This is our top monster of the day!

21:24.860 --> 21:28.020
I present it to the beautiful Lady Shamal!

21:28.020 --> 21:30.320
Thank you kindly.

21:30.320 --> 21:33.260
I present this to Lady Shamal, as well!

21:33.260 --> 21:35.900
I present this to Lady Shamal, as well!

21:36.170 --> 21:38.270
Thank you so much.

21:39.680 --> 21:42.400
<i>Noah's group is still out there?</i>

21:52.160 --> 21:54.160
Dame Ansley?!

21:55.180 --> 21:57.540
Dame Ansley, are you all right?

21:57.540 --> 21:59.170
Dame Ansley!

21:59.400 --> 22:03.420
Where are the others who were 
with you? What happened?

22:04.470 --> 22:07.080
H-Hell...

22:11.430 --> 22:13.050
Hell?

22:23.010 --> 22:24.270
Noah...

23:29.370 --> 23:31.370


23:35.010 --> 23:40.020
<b>Episode Eight</b>

23:35.010 --> 23:40.020
<b>Why Raeliana's Going to the Temple</b>
